* Generic single-pole rail-to-rail op-amp macro-model (behavioural).
* Aol = 100 dB, GBW = 10 MHz, output clamped 20 mV inside the rails, Rout = 50 ohm.
* Replace with the TI TLV9064 / TLV9062 SPICE model for sign-off simulations.
* Pins: inp inn out vcc vee
.subckt OPA_RR inp inn out vcc vee
Ein n1 0 inp inn 1e5
Rp  n1 n2 1k
Cp  n2 0 1.59u
* smooth (tanh) output limiter keeps DC convergence robust; loop gain absorbs the compression
Bo  no 0 V=(V(vcc)+V(vee))/2 + ((V(vcc)-V(vee))/2-0.02)*tanh((V(n2)-(V(vcc)+V(vee))/2)/((V(vcc)-V(vee))/2-0.02))
Ro  no out 50
.ends OPA_RR
